# Integrated Requirements for User Authentication

## General Overview
Develop a web application named 'CharitableGivingPlatform' that enables users to manage and contribute to charitable causes seamlessly using Python and local storage. The website should start from the login page.

## Software Functional Requirements

### User Authentication and Account Management

#### Login Page
1. Users shall be presented with an intuitive login form that requests a username and password.
2. The system shall validate the entered credentials against stored user information and grant access if they match.
3. In case of invalid credentials, users shall receive a clear and helpful error message guiding them on what to do next.

#### Registration Page
1. Users without an account can navigate to the Registration Page via a clearly visible "Register here" link on the Login Page.
2. The registration form shall collect essential personal information such as name, email address, and desired username and password.
3. Validation checks shall be implemented to ensure all required fields are completed and passwords meet complexity requirements.
4. Upon successful registration, users shall be automatically redirected to the Dashboard Page or receive a confirmation email with instructions to activate their account.

## Core Features
- Users shall be able to log in to their accounts on the Login Page by entering a username and password.
- Users shall be able to navigate to the Registration Page via the Register here link if they do not have an account.

## Data Storage
Data will be stored in local text files. Different types of data will be stored in separate `.txt` files. You should define the text file by yourself in advance. This structured data storage will facilitate easy data retrieval and management through simple file manipulations in Python, ensuring the application remains light and efficient without the need for a SQL database.

## Related Files
- `main.py`
- `templates/login.html`
- `templates/register.html`
- `users.txt`
